# requests-unit.list: the kvm-unit-tests that run each source of work the
# vCPU's request word drives before an entry (rach2/sys/kvm/Readme.md), in
# unit-tests.list's format, for the case unit-tests with the variable
# RACH2_KVM_UNIT: the local APIC and its timer, the PIT, Hyper-V's clock
# and synthetic timers, the kvmclock, the PMU, NMIs, INIT and SIPI, a
# halted vCPU's wake, and the exits whose handling 84-110 measured. EXPECT
# is unit-tests.list's.
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
x2apic outer_kvm?fail:pass|fail timeout Linux: timeout; duration=30; inside a machine of KVM nmi-after-sti fails, as under Linux 6.12 as the host there; elsewhere the clock decides TMCCT should not be reset to TMICT value, which reads the periodic count twice with a report line between and passes only when the line takes less than the count left or more than that and half a period: under the testing PC's TCG, with a period of 10.07 ms, the line took 11.3 ms on the milestone's head and passed, and 9.0 ms once exits were cheaper and failed
vmexit_tscdeadline pass pass
vmexit_tscdeadline_immed pass pass
vmexit_ipi_halt pass pass
vmexit_inl_pmtimer pass pass
eventinj pass pass
smptest pass pass
smptest3 pass pass
ioapic pass pass
hyperv_stimer pass pass
hyperv_stimer_direct pass pass
hyperv_synic pass pass
hyperv_clock pass pass
kvmclock_test pass pass
tsc pass pass
tsc_adjust pass pass
pmu kvm_pmu?hypervisor?fail:pass:skip fail Linux: AMD's overflow subtests fail, 7 to 10 of 10 by turns; under a hypervisor whose own work on each exit the counters count, the counts and overflows fail on Linux 6.12 too; skips without a host PMU, which its config requires
vmexit_cpuid pass pass
vmexit_vmcall pass pass
